{"kind":"assert","text":"C1 (21f6d3cd) takes one rule from the review of the client note\n(verdict 2123f760). The note has it in section 5.1 at c98b9a2c.\n\n1. `Custody` checks both bounds before it signs. A record that\n   holds 8 envelopes or 64 signings refuses a further signing:\n   `full`, reason `signings`. Nothing is signed. This check\n   stands beside the `full`, reason `bytes`, check of ruling\n   0767a3f9.\n2. `Custody` drops no envelope to make room. It drops an envelope\n   only when its signing is closed, and never the envelope of the\n   latest signing.\n3. A `refused` record keeps the envelope of its latest signing,\n   and of each earlier signing until that signing is closed. The\n   store keeps the record as it keeps each terminal record. State\n   in the C1 note how many terminal records each store keeps and\n   when one leaves. NF-5 states the same for the browser store.\n\nTests: nine submits inside one lifetime, each refused\n`revision-moved`. The ninth is refused `full` and signs nothing.\nAfter one signing closes, the next submit signs.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}